@startuml
title Lock / Unlock User Sequence (/api/admin/users/{id}/deactivate or restore)

autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Admin
boundary "Users Page\n(Dashboard)" as UsersPage
control "UsersController\n(Dashboard)" as DashboardUsersController
control "ServiceAPI\n(Dashboard)" as ServiceApi
control "AdminUsersController\n(API)" as AdminUsersController
control "AdminUserService" as AdminUserService
control "AdminUserRepository" as AdminUserRepository
database "VocaNovaDbContext" as DbContext
database "MySQL Database" as MySQL

note over UsersPage, MySQL
Checked in current code:
Dashboard uses POST /users/{id}/deactivate or /restore.
ServiceAPI calls PATCH /api/admin/users/{id}/deactivate or /restore.
No request DTO body is used; API returns bool in the response envelope.
end note

Admin -> UsersPage: Click Lock/Unlock user
UsersPage -> DashboardUsersController: POST /users/{id}/deactivate\nor /users/{id}/restore
DashboardUsersController -> ServiceApi: DeactivateUserAsync(id)\nor RestoreUserAsync(id)
ServiceApi -> AdminUsersController: PATCH /api/admin/users/{id}/deactivate\nor /api/admin/users/{id}/restore
AdminUsersController -> AdminUsersController: Check admin authorization
AdminUsersController -> AdminUserService: DeactivateAsync(id, actorRole)\nor RestoreAsync(id, actorRole)

AdminUserService -> AdminUserRepository: GetStatusTargetAsync(id)
AdminUserRepository -> DbContext: Query target user status and role
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT user status and role
MySQL --> DbContext: Target row or null
DbContext --> AdminUserRepository: Result
AdminUserRepository --> AdminUserService: Status target or null

alt User not found
    AdminUserService --> AdminUsersController: NotFound result
    AdminUsersController --> ServiceApi: HTTP 404 error
    ServiceApi --> DashboardUsersController: Action failed
    DashboardUsersController --> UsersPage: Show feedback
else User cannot be managed
    AdminUserService --> AdminUsersController: Forbidden/Conflict result
    AdminUsersController --> ServiceApi: HTTP 403/409 error
    ServiceApi --> DashboardUsersController: Action failed
    DashboardUsersController --> UsersPage: Show feedback
else User can be managed
    AdminUserService -> AdminUserRepository: StageStatusAsync(id, locked/active)
    AdminUserRepository -> DbContext: Update user status
    DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE users
    MySQL --> DbContext: Update result

    opt Lock user
        AdminUserService -> AdminUserRepository: RevokeActiveRefreshTokensAsync(id)
        AdminUserRepository -> DbContext: Revoke active refresh tokens
        DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE refresh_tokens
        MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
    end

    AdminUserService -> AdminUserRepository: SaveChangesAsync()
    AdminUserRepository -> DbContext: Save changes
    DbContext --> AdminUserRepository: Save result
    AdminUserRepository --> AdminUserService: Saved
    AdminUserService --> AdminUsersController: Success result
    AdminUsersController --> ServiceApi: HTTP 200 OK
    ServiceApi --> DashboardUsersController: Action success
    DashboardUsersController --> UsersPage: Show feedback and refresh page
end

@enduml
